content.text:
Now main.js.

Need imports: Game, UI, AudioEngine, Input, data SAVE_KEY, STARTER_WEAPONS, getWeapon maybe. `BIOMES`? no.

Default meta. Merge with loaded. Need ensure all deep fields.

Meta normalization:
```
function defaultMeta() {
 const collection = Object.fromEntries(STARTER_WEAPONS.map(id=>[id,1]));
 return {...}
}
function loadMeta() {
 const raw = localStorage.getItem(SAVE_KEY);
 if (!raw) return default;
 try { const data=JSON.parse(raw); return normalize(data); } catch { return def; }
}
function normalize(data){
 const d=defaultMeta();
 const m={...d,...data, stats:{...d.stats,...(data.stats||{})}, materials:{...d.materials,...(data.materials||{})}, ...}
 settings merge, potions merge, echo merge, skills merge, upgrades merge, collection merge.
 ensure ownedWeapons includes starters? maybe not; if old save. Ensure equipped weapon valid.
 equippedSkills = array of 2, filter invalid? Keep.
 clamp levels.
}
```
Need include `name`.

Save function:
```
let saveTimer; function saveMeta(meta){ localStorage.setItem(...) }
```
Throttle? Game calls save often (enterRoom, loot). localStorage sync small. Fine. Also on visibility/unload.

Create audio = new AudioEngine(meta.settings), input = new Input(canvas), ui = new UI(audio,input), game = new Game(canvas, ui, audio, input, meta, saveMeta); ui.game=game; ui.refreshMute(); game.goTitle(); game.start(); ui.hideBoot();

But Input constructed before UI? It sets up joystick listeners on DOMContentLoaded; script is module at end of body, DOM loaded. fine.

Potential issue Game constructor calls deriveStats reading `this.run?.weaponId || m.equippedWeapon`. Good.

Set canvas focus? no.

Boot hide after game started. Could hide after 500ms.

Debug:
```
window.__SKPA__ = { game, ui, audio, input, save: saveMeta };
window.game = game; window.ui=ui; window.meta=meta? 
```
Maybe expose getters. For automation, window.__SKPA__.

